                                                1. OSI Model Layers & Functions
=======================================================================================================================================
The **OSI (Open Systems Interconnection) Model** is a conceptual framework that explains how data travels from one device to
another across a network.

## OSI Model (7 Layers)

| Layer | Name         | Function                                 | Example               |
| ----- | ------------ | ---------------------------------------- | --------------------- |
| 7     | Application  | User interaction with network services   | HTTP, FTP, SMTP       |
| 6     | Presentation | Data formatting, encryption, compression | SSL/TLS, JPEG         |
| 5     | Session      | Establishes and manages sessions         | NetBIOS, RPC          |
| 4     | Transport    | End-to-end communication                 | TCP, UDP              |
| 3     | Network      | Routing and logical addressing           | IP, ICMP              |
| 2     | Data Link    | Physical addressing and frame transfer   | MAC, Ethernet         |
| 1     | Physical     | Transmission of bits over media          | Cables, Wi-Fi signals |
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Data Encapsulation Process

When sending data:
```
Application Data
      ↓
TCP Header Added
      ↓
IP Header Added
      ↓
Ethernet Header Added
      ↓
Bits Sent Across Network
```
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Cybersecurity Perspective

| Layer        | Attack Examples    |
| ------------ | ------------------ |
| Application  | SQL Injection, XSS |
| Presentation | SSL/TLS attacks    |
| Session      | Session Hijacking  |
| Transport    | TCP SYN Flood      |
| Network      | IP Spoofing        |
| Data Link    | MAC Flooding       |
| Physical     | Cable Tapping      |
