                                                     2. TCP/IP Protocol Suite
=======================================================================================================================================
The TCP/IP Model is the practical networking model used on the Internet.

## TCP/IP Layers

| TCP/IP Layer   | Equivalent OSI Layers |
| -------------- | --------------------- |
| Application    | OSI 5,6,7             |
| Transport      | OSI 4                 |
| Internet       | OSI 3                 |
| Network Access | OSI 1,2               |
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## TCP/IP Architecture

```text
+--------------------+
| Application Layer  |
+--------------------+
| Transport Layer    |
+--------------------+
| Internet Layer     |
+--------------------+
| Network Access     |
+--------------------+
```
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Important Protocols

### Application Layer

| Protocol | Port | Purpose             |
| -------- | ---- | ------------------- |
| HTTP     | 80   | Web traffic         |
| HTTPS    | 443  | Secure web traffic  |
| FTP      | 21   | File transfer       |
| SSH      | 22   | Secure remote login |
| SMTP     | 25   | Email sending       |
| DNS      | 53   | Domain resolution   |

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Transport Layer
#### TCP (Transmission Control Protocol)

Characteristics:

* Connection-oriented
* Reliable
* Error checking
* Ordered delivery

Examples:

```
HTTPS
SSH
FTP
SMTP
```
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#### UDP (User Datagram Protocol)

Characteristics:
* Connectionless
* Faster
* No delivery guarantee

Examples:

```
DNS
VoIP
Streaming
Gaming
```
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## TCP Three-Way Handshake

Before communication starts:

```text
Client             Server

SYN      -------->

          <-------- SYN-ACK

ACK      -------->
```

Connection established.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## TCP Flags

| Flag | Meaning          |
| ---- | ---------------- |
| SYN  | Start connection |
| ACK  | Acknowledgment   |
| FIN  | End connection   |
| RST  | Reset connection |
| PSH  | Push data        |
| URG  | Urgent data      |
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Cybersecurity Importance

Attackers frequently abuse:

* SYN Flood
* TCP Reset Attacks
* Session Hijacking
* Port Scanning

Tools:
```
nmap
wireshark
tcpdump
hping3
```
