# DNS (Domain Name System)

DNS translates domain names into IP addresses.

Example:

```text
www.google.com
     ↓
142.250.xxx.xxx
``
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Why DNS Exists

Humans remember:
```
google.com
facebook.com
```

Computers use:
```
142.250.182.46
157.240.229.35
```

DNS performs the translation.
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

## DNS Resolution Process

```text
User Browser
      ↓
Local DNS Resolver
      ↓
Root Server
      ↓
TLD Server (.com)
      ↓
Authoritative DNS Server
      ↓
IP Address Returned
```
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## Common DNS Records

| Record | Purpose           |
| ------ | ----------------- |
| A      | IPv4 Address      |
| AAAA   | IPv6 Address      |
| MX     | Mail Server       |
| NS     | Name Server       |
| TXT    | Verification Info |
| CNAME  | Alias             |
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
## DNS Security Attacks

| Attack               | Description        |
| -------------------- | ------------------ |
| DNS Spoofing         | Fake DNS responses |
| Cache Poisoning      | Corrupt DNS cache  |
| DNS Tunneling        | Data exfiltration  |
| Amplification Attack | DDoS using DNS     |
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
